mm37 end parks, on top of the LIVE Shield runtime's wasi-nn ggml backend (crates/wasi-nn/src/backend/ggml.rs
c3cbac2c, the tree recorded in isolation/m4/evidence/eyesoff-ttft-2026-09-29/runtime-build.json: wasmtime f7d3104c).
Built in that tree's own cargo cache (same command and ELL_LIB_LOCATION, see runtime-build.json) -> wasmtime 2936ad79.

A guest may ask ({"park_end": [1]}, caps[19] = 1) for its sequence to be parked WHOLE when the session ends - prompt
plus everything generated - so the conversation's next turn, whose prompt replays that answer as its exact ids,
branches off its end instead of re-reading it. Per-sequence token shadows on the server follow every cache change
(submit, verify, mtp_round, rewind, copy, branch, fork, eviction); a poisoned or mismatched shadow never parks. A
session ending inside a fused mtp_round has its unchecked drafts trimmed (within the snapshot depth) first.
ENCLAVE_GGML_PARK_TRACE=1 explains each decision on stderr (off by default; counts only, never tokens).

